summary:
  The length a buffer's header was written with is taken for the place the reader stood at.

history:
  Measured 2026-11-12: a station at an address with no ending, Ogg Vorbis and
  plain FLAC alike, is kept in a Matroska file whose header names the whole
  window as its length. Fourteen seconds of play, a pause of four, Play: 3.6 s
  later the reader met the file's unfinished end, the player gave its position
  as 300000 ms against 22 s captured, and the station went back to the
  broadcast with the pause lost.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TimeshiftLogic.js

find:
      if (typeof posMs === "number" && typeof capturedMs === "number" && posMs >= 0 && posMs <= capturedMs) return posMs;

replace:
      if (typeof posMs === "number" && typeof capturedMs === "number" && posMs >= 0) return posMs;

expect:
  Killed by tst_timeshiftlogic::test_the_end_of_a_single_file_is_where_the_reader_stood.
  Line-neutral.
